  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tarneeb. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Tarneeb (Arabic for 'Trump') is a popular trick-taking card game in the Middle East (Levant, Egypt). It is a partnership game for 4 players. Teams bid on how many tricks they can take (starting from 7 up to 13). The highest bidder names the trump suit (Tarneeb). The objective is to fulfill the bid.",
    objective: 'Win at least as many tricks as bid. First team to reach target score (e.g., 31, 41, or 61) wins.',
    gameplay: "Bidding starts at 7 tricks. Players bid number of tricks (7-13) or pass. Highest bidder declares Trump (Tarneeb). Player to dealer's right (or bidder) leads first. Must follow suit. Highest trump wins, or highest card of led suit. Winner leads next.",
